abstract: >-
  An evidence-driven Quality Engineering framework for evaluating autonomous
  and agentic systems across outcomes, trajectories, tool use, safety,
  reliability and efficiency. The work covers versioned evaluation datasets,
  normalized traces, deterministic-first task/tool/argument/sequence checks,
  groundedness, authorization and approvals, recovery, repeated-run stability,
  latency and cost, calibrated LLM judges, human evaluation, baseline
  regression, risk-based CI/CD profiles, hard quality gates, missing-evidence
  handling, observability and production-to-regression learning.